Re: [SparkR-SQL] unit test failure after integration of PR that implements subtract() and subtractByKey() <https://sparkr.atlassian.net/browse/SPARKR-244>

Yeah but I don't think it necessarily means that we should use `except`. For one I think its better to have fewer keywords users need to know and sharing same name is probably better. Anyways thats a different discussion – Lets fix this test case now by using `except` and we'll revisit this when we audit the API before 1.4 release.

